# Resources/markdown-viewer holds vendored third-party runtime bundles (mermaid,
# vega, highlight.js) plus the generated webviews React app build (the diff
# viewer, its highlight worker and the lazy Shiki grammar/theme/WASM chunks).
# They are not authored source, so exclude them from GitHub Linguist's
# language stats.
Resources/markdown-viewer/** linguist-vendored
Resources/markdown-viewer/webviews-app/** linguist-generated

# Xcode string catalogs are one large JSON object keyed by string id. Two
# branches that each add a different key collide positionally, producing dozens
# of conflict hunks with no semantic disagreement. scripts/merge-xcstrings.py
# merges per key and writes an ordinary conflict whenever both sides changed the
# same key. Register it with scripts/install-git-hooks.sh (run by setup.sh);
# without that config git silently uses the default driver.
*.xcstrings merge=xcstrings-v2

# A merge can run right after checking out a fork branch, so a driver resolved
# from the working tree would run that branch's code with the maintainer's
# credentials. scripts/install-git-hooks.sh installs reviewed copies into
# $GIT_COMMON_DIR/cmux-merge-drivers and configures absolute paths to those, so
# what git executes is not what a branch can rewrite; it also repoints the
# older checkout-relative merge.xcstrings name at the same trusted copy.
# scripts/ci/catch_up_pr.py pins every driver to false instead, since catch-up
# only needs to know which paths are unmerged.

# The Xcode project file collides the same way, and for a sharper reason: no
# target here is filesystem-synchronized, so adding one source file writes four
# entries, and two branches adding different files append to all four of the
# same regions. scripts/merge-pbxproj.py takes the union of entries each side
# added and writes an ordinary conflict whenever a hunk is anything else. Same
# registration.
cmux.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj merge=pbxproj-v1

# Generated files that two branches always collide in. Line merging cannot
# combine two builds; the only right result is a rebuild of the merged sources.
# `cmux-generated-v1` keeps the current branch's copy so the merge finishes,
# then scripts/cmux-next/regenerate-web-bundles.sh rebuilds what is still
# committed and CI's checks fail until it has.
# The web bundles themselves (agent pane, Activity, palette ranker, webviews app,
# pages) are build output since cx-vn5 and gitignored, and the strings tables
# since #21946; their lines stay so the
# generated catch-up still treats a merge with an older branch, whose only
# conflicts are those deleted bundles, as generated (regenerate-web-bundles.sh
# removes them from the index). The driver command is `true`, a git
# no-op that runs no checked-out code. Register it with
# scripts/install-git-hooks.sh. GitHub ignores merge drivers, so a PR still
# shows the conflict until its branch is merged locally. The driver runs no
# code, but it does keep one side: a branch that names another path here
# would have that path's incoming changes dropped when a configured clone
# merges into it. Review additions to these lines like a revert.
# Every file the agent pane and Agent Activity builds write, not only index.html:
# pane.js, the highlight worker and the per-locale string loaders collide too.
Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/Sources/CmuxNextAgentPane/Resources/agent-pane/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/Sources/CmuxNextAgentActivity/Resources/agent-activity/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/Sources/CmuxNextPalette/Resources/palette-ranker.js merge=cmux-generated-v1
Resources/markdown-viewer/webviews-app/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
# The React pages (build-pages-web.sh) and the strings tables it generates from the
# xcstrings catalogs. Only generated output; the page sources merge normally.
Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/Sources/CmuxNextPages/Resources/pages/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
# gen-strings.mjs writes every strings table, the agent pane's included (build
# output since #21946).
webviews/src/**/generated/strings.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
webviews/src/pages/home-channels/generated/pane-strings.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
webviews/src/pages/diff/generated/locales/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
webviews/src/pages/diff/generated/localeLoaders.ts merge=cmux-generated-v1
# The other exports scripts/ci/next_batch.py's merger rebuilds (its
# SWIFT_GENERATED and SDK_GENERATED; tests/test_install_git_hooks.py checks
# that every kept path is one of them). A kept copy that is stale fails its
# --check until it is regenerated: regenerate-swift-exports.sh for the Swift
# ones, cmux-tui/bindings/codegen/generate.py for the SDK. Generated files
# without that rebuild (the app-host and cloud-wire code, the docs shortcuts,
# the AppPlatform permission scopes) merge by line, so a lost change conflicts
# instead of being dropped.
plans/cmux-next/action-surfaces.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
plans/cmux-next/actions.md merge=cmux-generated-v1
plans/cmux-next/links.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
schemas/settings/settings-schema.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
docs/mdm/com.manaflow.cmux.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
docs/mdm/com.manaflow.cmux.plist merge=cmux-generated-v1
docs/mdm/com.manaflow.cmux.intune.plist merge=cmux-generated-v1
docs/mdm/managed-preferences.md merge=cmux-generated-v1
# The settings source stamp merges by line on GitHub (an entry per source, so
# two settings pull requests do not conflict there, #21946). A configured clone
# keeps one side like the exports above, so a local merge of two settings
# branches fails defaults_guard.py check-fresh until the exports are
# regenerated; a line-merged stamp would call the one-side exports fresh. After
# a GitHub merge the base autofix regenerates them (it runs whenever
# CmuxNextSettings changed).
Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/ci-target-graph.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
# SDK wire layers (cmux-tui/bindings/codegen/generate.py): only the wholly
# generated directories and files; go/raw and java mix in hand-written code.
cmux-tui/bindings/go/raw/.cmux-sdk-manifest.json merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/python/cmux/raw/_generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/cpp/include/cmux/raw/generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/cpp/src/raw/generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/go/raw/generated_*.go merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/typescript/src/raw/generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/rust/src/generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
cmux-tui/bindings/zig/src/raw/generated/** merge=cmux-generated-v1
# The daemon capability export (DaemonCapabilityExportTests) is one sorted
# array per list. Keeping one side whole dropped the other side's new entries
# on rebases (cx-urd.9.3), so scripts/merge-daemon-capabilities.py merges each
# list as a set and conflicts only on a capability that ends in two lists.
# Same trusted registration as xcstrings-v2; an unconfigured clone merges it
# by line, which conflicts instead of dropping an entry.
plans/cmux-next/daemon-capabilities.json merge=cmux-capabilities-v1
# Ratchet baselines list known debt per entry. Keeping one side whole would
# drop the other side's fixes (style ratchets only warn under their ceiling),
# so scripts/merge-baseline.py merges entry by entry and writes a conflict only
# when both sides changed the same entry. Same trusted registration as
# xcstrings-v2.
scripts/lint-namespace-types-ratchet.txt merge=cmux-baseline-v1
scripts/lint-namespace-types-baseline.txt merge=cmux-baseline-v1
scripts/lint-ios-package-conventions-baseline.txt merge=cmux-baseline-v1
scripts/cmux-next/*-baseline.tsv merge=cmux-baseline-v1
scripts/cmux-next/*-baseline.json merge=cmux-baseline-v1
# Upstream license texts the shared Ghostty license collector ships, pinned by
# SHA-256 in pinned-licenses/MANIFEST.json. Never rewrite their bytes.
cmux-tui/build-support/notices/ghostty/pinned-licenses/** -text -whitespace
cmux-tui/build-support/notices/texts/** -text -whitespace
